timeline.body:
Check the logger value before going through all the effort of assembling the string, which can be costly.
```
Level level = ExceptionsHelper.status(throwable).getStatus() >= 500 ? Level.WARN : Level.DEBUG;
if (logger.isLevel(level)) {
   // assemble string
  logger.log(level, message)
```

Additionally you can use the supplier as long as the exception is accepted:
`logger.log(level, () -> LoggingUtils.createLoggingMessage(error, queryName, throwable, preamble), throwable)`

The advantage of the latter is separating the error message creation from logging.

